## Context

Author decision (Imagine, 2026-11-09, session in `~/CNRS/missions` on the
return from Jéco Lyon and MeSSH Condorcet): one travel lifecycle skill,
sibling of `/paper` (ticket 1483), not one skill per step. Name `/mission`
settled 2026-11-09 after a naming round (mission, roam, range, wing,
swoop, sortie): the skills that manage an object of the trade carry the
object's name, mirroring its directory (`missions/` → `/mission`,
`papiers/` → `/paper`); the dragon verbs stay for the harness's skills on
itself.

Reference: REALF chapter 7 « How to present your work », How-to 35–39
(`~/CNRS/papiers/actif/REALF 2025 édition/main.pdf`, p. 52–57): choose a
venue, pack the bag, attend, wrap up after an event, get a refund. The
chapter is the rationale; the checklists are derived from the harness
infrastructure and the author's filing conventions, not copied.

The author's own wrap-up list, in three strands (2026-11-09):
- CNRS: declare the return, claim the refund, hand over the receipts,
  make sure the mission is findable for the RIBAC.
- CIRED: write and share a brief compte rendu.
- Self: archive the communication on the personal page and HAL, update
  the year's roadmap.

Gap found: no skill mentions missions. `/update-publist` covers page +
HAL, the `email` skill covers sending, `/submission-event` (→ `/paper`)
knows the roadmap for manuscripts only. Nothing covers the ordre de
mission, the état de frais, the receipts, the compte rendu, or the move
to `done/`. The only tool reading `missions/` is
`~/CNRS/code/activity_report_writer/ribac-check`, with hard-coded paths
`missions/done/Conférences`, `missions/done/Cours`,
`missions/actif/keynote`.

## Filing conventions observed (to encode, not to change)

- `missions/actif/AAAA-MM-JJ Événement/`, `missions/done/<rubrique>/Ville
  AAAA-MM-JJ Événement/` with seven rubriques (Conférences, Séminaires,
  Cours, Project meetings, GIEC, Jurikomités, Field trips), plus
  `missions/annulees/` and `missions/annonce/`. The move to `done/`
  implies a rename and a rubrique choice; the rubrique decides whether
  ribac-check sees it.
- Model folder: `missions/actif/2026-09-18 Mahdia/` — README with a table
  of subfolders, `voyage/` (ordre de mission, bookings, cancellations),
  `sources/`, the production folder, and a « Suite » section declaring
  the folder closed with the compte rendu mail archived as Markdown.
- Frozen outputs in a dated `release/<AAAA-MM-JJ>/` subfolder (Jéco:
  `release/2026-11-01/publication/` holds the HAL deposit and homepage
  result), per the CNRS filing convention memory
  (`~/.claude/projects/-home-haduong-CNRS/memory/project-cnrs-filing-convention.md`).
- Secretariat side: `~/CNRS/secretariat/procedures/Formulaires missions/`
  (état de frais, instruction missions), roadmap `~/CNRS/secretariat/Feuille
  de route <year>.odt` section « 2. Communications ».

## Design

- `skills/mission/SKILL.md` is a short router: argument `<dossier> <stage>`,
  stage ∈ `prepare | check | return`; it resolves the dossier under
  `missions/actif/`, reads its README if any, then loads
  `references/<stage>.md`. Venue choice stays with `/choose-venue`;
  abstracts with `/conference-submission-prep`; the talk's content with
  `/message-framing` and `/slides`; a manuscript event met during a
  mission goes to `/paper`.
- `references/prepare.md` (How-to 35, 36 first half, 39 first half):
  create the dossier with `voyage/` and README; estimate and ordre de
  mission (Etamine) as author-only items; bookings through the lab's
  procedures, never bought by hand; registration receipt filed; roadmap
  row created in « Communications »; calendar entry.
- `references/check.md` (How-to 36 second half, 37): the bag list, paper
  and electronic; slides sent to organisers and chair the night before;
  session brief (day, slot, chair, co-speakers, announced title) in one
  page; talking points; contacts looked up through `directory`.
- `references/return.md` (How-to 38, 39): the three strands above as
  three sections, each with its register, its delegate and its
  author-only gate. CNRS: receipts inventoried in `voyage/`, état de frais
  as an explicit stop (browser + signature, the skill prepares the list
  and hands back). CIRED: compte rendu drafted from the dossier, Mahdia
  mail as the shape, sent via `email` on confirmation, archived in the
  dossier. Self: communication PDF through `/update-publist` (page then
  HAL), roadmap row updated, dated `release/` subfolder with the
  authentic artifacts (provenance step, hash them), LinkedIn post as an
  author-only item. Close: README « Suite » section, move to
  `done/<rubrique>/Ville AAAA-MM-JJ Événement`, and extend ribac-check's
  path list if the rubrique is not Conférences or Cours.
- Each checklist states: register(s) touched; provenance step; filesystem
  steps; outward gates named with who clicks; delegates; author-only items
  listed so they are asked, not dropped. Same section skeleton as `/paper`
  so the two skills read alike.

## Worked examples for the `return` stage (state on 2026-11-09)

- Jéco Lyon, 3 novembre 2026: tribune on the page and on HAL
  (hal-05847469, in moderation), roadmap row written, outbound ticket
  and Airbnb receipt in the folder, no return ticket, no état de frais,
  no compte rendu, folder still in `actif/`.
- MeSSH Campus Condorcet, 9 juillet 2026: slides `slides-messh26-cirdi.pdf`
  not indexed on page or HAL (only the Cirdi final report of December
  2025 is), roadmap row says « écrire un billet », registration
  confirmation only, no compte rendu, folder still in `actif/`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] An AGENTS.md in ~/CNRS/missions/ holds what is local (conventions, places, preferences), the skill reads it and holds only the stages, routing and gates. Content: naming in `actif/` and `done/<rubrique>/`, the seven rubriques, where the secretariat forms are, the paths `ribac-check` reads, local preferences.
- [ ] `skills/mission/SKILL.md` router and three checklists in
      `skills/mission/references/`, catalog updated, hygiene tests pass
- [ ] Each checklist carries the six sections (registers, provenance,
      filesystem, gates with who clicks, delegates, author-only items)
- [ ] `/mission "2026-07-09 MeSSH Campus Condorcet" return` dry run lists
      the slides indexing, the compte rendu, the move to
      `done/Conférences/Paris 2026-07-09 MeSSH` and nothing the agent had
      to discover
- [ ] `/mission "2026-09-18 Mahdia" return` dry run lands on « nothing to
      do » (positive control: the folder is the model)
- [ ] `make check` passes
